WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.970
Every Christmas Eve,

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.170
certain traditions say that
Santa has just one night

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.810
to deliver presents to
millions of children

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.280
around the globe.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.430
Now, this might seem unreasonable

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.650
from a scientific perspective.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.075
But we wondered, exactly
how unreasonable is it?

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.980
Overall, it's difficult to determine

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.790
how many people around the world

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.510
celebrate a Santa-centric
Christmas on December 25th.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.460
But if we consider certain religious

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.780
and cultural traditions,

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.850
we get a rough estimate of
about 600 million people.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.460
Now, let's say each
household has, on average,

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.150
two and a half kids.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.760
So Santa only needs to
visit 240 million homes.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.480
Even better? He has more
time to get the job done

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.040
than you might think.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.410
Legend has it that he drops
by when the kids are asleep.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.240
So that gives him eight hours, right?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.940
Well, hold up.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.700
We mustn't forget about time zones.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.766
There are 24 broad time zones worldwide,

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.910
each one hour apart.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:13.220
So factor in the different
Christmas Eve start times

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.620
across the planet,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.040
and Kringle's got a luxurious 31 hours

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.060
to make his deliveries.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.120
Unfortunately, this is
where his luck runs out.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.720
Because just to reach every house,

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.780
he'll have to fly 1,200 times faster

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.650
than the world's fastest jet fighter.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.620
That's a lot to ask of nine reindeer,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.900
which can only gallop

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.840
up to 80 kilometers per hour
on average. Way too slow.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:42.950
But to be fair,

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.400
that's the best they can do on the ground.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.230
Since we don't know exactly
how fast a reindeer can fly,

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.570
let's assume they can manage
those incredible speeds.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.980
Even then, the load they have to lug

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.240
is much too heavy for them.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.030
If every kid receives a
single mid-sized Lego set,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.150
the bag alone would weigh
a whopping 600,000 tons,

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.870
or about 20 Statue of Liberties.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:09.820
Meanwhile, the average reindeer

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.310
can pull up to twice their
weight, or about 225 kilograms.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.070
So those deer aren't going anywhere.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.370
And even if they could,

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.290
well, it wouldn't be pretty.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:26.780
For starters, the team would
create a massive sonic boom

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.970
as they hurdle through the
air at 3,000 times faster

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:31.720
than the speed of sound,

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.210
deafening any bystanders
on the ground below.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.290
Merry Christmas folks!

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.980
But it gets worse.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.380
Once Rudolph and Co. take off,

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.320
they vaporize before they
reach their first house.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.560
Just like how a rocket heats up

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.000
when it reenters the atmosphere
at tremendous speeds,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.760
the reindeer would heat
to blistering temperatures

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.490
that would turn them into venison jerky.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.200
And Santa wouldn't fare much better

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.410
because he's sitting

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.490
on what amounts to the worst
roller-coaster ride on Earth.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.940
When a typical coaster accelerates,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.440
you get pushed back against your seat.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.880
But in Santa's case,

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.450
to accelerate to those extreme speeds

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.300
makes for a much stronger push.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.470
A force tens of thousands of times

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.520
stronger than gravity
would pin into the sleigh,

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.210
smashing his bones and
internal organs to jelly.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.700
But it's not all doom and gloom.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.470
Let's assume Santa and friends

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:31.960
miraculously survive this ordeal.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.840
He slips his conveniently boneless body

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.890
through chimney after chimney,

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.390
drops off the gifts,

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.830
and now gets to munch on
his well-deserved treats.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.820
A lot of treats.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.870
If every household offers
him three sugar cookies

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.560
and one 8-ounce glass of whole milk,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.140
that's 720 million cookies

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:56.980
and enough milk to fill 23
Olympic swimming pools total.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.479
Now, that adds up to

00:03:59.479 --> 00:04:02.904
396 billion calories.

00:04:02.904 --> 00:04:06.100
Plenty to see him through his hibernation

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.017
until Christmas comes round again.

